  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will build\nnorthward over the Silver State this afternoon. This ridge of \nhigh pressure will progress eastward tonight and Thursday. High \ntemperatures across Northern and Central Nevada both this\nafternoon and Thursday afternoon will be around ten degrees above\nnormal for this time of year. An Eastern Pacific storm system \nwill approach the west coast of the United States Friday. As a \nresult, the surface pressure gradient will increase. Sustained \nsouth winds 20 to 30 mph, with gusts near 50 mph are expected in\nNorthern and Central Nevada Friday and Friday night. A Wind \nAdvisory is in effect from 10 AM PST Friday morning until 3 AM \nPST early Saturday morning.\n\nA trough of low pressure will pass eastward across Northern and\nCentral Nevada Friday afternoon through Saturday morning,\nresulting in periods of precipitation. Snow levels will\nstart at around 8,000 feet Friday afternoon, before dropping to \nabout 5,500 feet by Saturday morning. Here are probabilities of\none quarter of an inch of liquid precipitation or more Friday\nafternoon and Friday night:\n\nWinnemucca - 67%\nAustin - 65%\nEureka - 60%\nBattle Mountain - 57%\nCarlin - 57%\nElko - 55%\nSpring Creek - 53%\nOwyhee - 53%\nEly - 47%\nTonopah - 41%\n\nThere will be a brief break in precipitation the remainder of the\nupcoming weekend, prior to the next storm system Monday morning through\nTuesday afternoon. Snow levels will start at around 7,000 feet\nMonday morning, before dropping to about 5,000 feet Monday night.\nHere are probabilities of 0.1 inches of snowfall or more for \nselect locations in Northern and Central Nevada Monday night into \nTuesday morning:\n \nAustin - 75%\nRuth - 75%\nLamoille - 70%\nEureka - 65%\nMcGill - 65%\nSpring Creek - 60%\nOwyhee - 60%\nEly - 55%\nJackpot - 55%\nElko - 20%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding unseasonably warm weather both this afternoon and\nThursday afternoon. High forecast confidence in strong wind gusts\nFriday and Friday night. High forecast confidence regarding\nperiods of precipitation Friday afternoon through Saturday\nmorning. Moderate forecast confidence in periods of precipitation\nMonday morning through Tuesday afternoon. No deviations from the\nNBM model output.",
